Lobium - navigator.webdriver answered natively, not by a command-line flag.

The launcher used to pass --disable-blink-features=AutomationControlled to keep this false
(measured: true without it, false with it). That worked, and cost two tells to buy it: Chromium
raises a yellow "You are using an unsupported command-line flag" infobar for it on every launch,
and the flag names itself on chrome://version. Both are visible to the person using the browser and
to anything reading the page, on a product whose whole purpose is not looking automated.

This answers the surface where every other fingerprint surface is answered - inside Blink, gated on
the profile carrying a Lobium config - so the flag is redundant and has been removed from
packages/engine-runner/src/launch.ts.

diff --git a/third_party/blink/renderer/core/frame/navigator.cc b/third_party/blink/renderer/core/frame/navigator.cc
index 583f05f8dd5fb..7034bf4104734 100644
--- a/third_party/blink/renderer/core/frame/navigator.cc
+++ b/third_party/blink/renderer/core/frame/navigator.cc
@@ -23,6 +23,8 @@
 
 #include "third_party/blink/renderer/core/frame/navigator.h"
 
+#include "components/lobium_fp/lobium_fp_config.h"
+
 #include "third_party/blink/renderer/bindings/core/v8/script_controller.h"
 #include "third_party/blink/renderer/core/dom/document.h"
 #include "third_party/blink/renderer/core/execution_context/navigator_base.h"
@@ -98,6 +100,16 @@ bool Navigator::cookieEnabled() const {
 }
 
 bool Navigator::webdriver() const {
+  // Lobium: navigator.webdriver is a fingerprint surface, so it is answered HERE rather than by a
+  // command-line flag. The launcher used to pass --disable-blink-features=AutomationControlled to
+  // get the same false, which cost two things: Chromium showed the user a yellow "unsupported
+  // command-line flag" infobar on every launch, and the flag itself is listed on chrome://version
+  // - an automation tell on a browser whose whole purpose is not looking automated. A profile
+  // running under the Lobium config is a real user's browser and says so.
+  if (lobium::LobiumFpConfig::Current()) {
+    return false;
+  }
+
   if (RuntimeEnabledFeatures::AutomationControlledEnabled())
     return true;
 
